# A lambda parameter may not carry a default value.
#
# A default is evaluated in the scope the definition is written in, at
# each call that omits the argument (PYKING.md, "Default parameters").
# A lambda is an expression written wherever it stands, so it has no
# such scope to speak of, and only a `def` parameter may have one.
#
# This program is expected to FAIL parsing. Its `.ast.out` holds the
# error message, not a program's output.

f = (x = 1) => x
print(f(2))
